     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. The dose is well above the safe range for metformin.\n\n- **Ordered:** 1700 mg three times daily, which is 5,100 mg/day.\n- **Maximum labeled dose:** 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release in many labels. Single doses are usually 500\u20131,000 mg, and 850 mg is the largest common tablet strength.\n- **Risk:** This is about twice the maximum daily dose. It raises the risk of severe GI toxicity and lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nOrders like this should come from the prescribing clinician. It's possible a digit was mistyped, for example 850 mg or 1000 mg instead of 1700 mg.\n\nIf the prescriber confirms a corrected dose, I can enter it right away. Examples are 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day) or 500\u20131000 mg PO twice daily with meals. Please send me the confirmed dose and frequency, ideally from the prescriber. If the 1700 mg dose was intended, the prescriber should review it with pharmacy first."
      }
